  the next pass decides: the grader said a person must settle: src/build/followup-ticket.ts copies each grader gap into the follow-up ticket word for word. #lp-prod-judge tells the grader to name the file and line in each gap (for example 'src/build/grade.ts:12'), so the follow-up tickets will usually name file paths, and #st-ticket says a ticket names no file paths. The cards conflict: #st-grade-defer says to quote each gap as the grader wrote it. A person must decide whether follow-up tickets are exempt from the no-file-paths rule, or whether paths are taken out of the quoted gaps.; src/build/file-followup.ts appends ticket.planned for the follow-up without running the own-ticket checks. #st-ticket-partial says a ticket that fails its own checks gets no ticket.planned event. A follow-up whose quoted gaps contain file paths, or that is longer than 4000 characters, still goes on the board. If the checks run, such a follow-up never reaches the board, and that defeats #st-grade-defer. A person must decide which rule wins for follow-up tickets: run the checks and drop the follow-up, change the quoted text, or exempt follow-ups.
